Z||000002||Doni Hagan||09-18-2001||12:33 AM||||Sometimes a psychological diversion is the best thing for a person. If I lived in New York, I'd sure as hell want to get my mind off things as well, if only for a moment. What better way than to concentrate on a car?<BR>It's not denial, just a respite.<P>Very non-threatening and comforting. ||||reg||5
Z||000003||Wolfhound||09-18-2001||06:48 AM||||What you may be seeing is people going for repair before replacement. Hard to read a lot into this, but I sand and finish floors and in a good economic period the percentage of new floors seems to increase over refinish work and vise versa, a reflection of new housing. ||||reg||1
